WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.060
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.730
Today we are going to make some crazy synthetic
music videos.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:15.580
In machine learning research, view synthesis
papers are on the rise these days.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:20.949
These techniques are also referred to as NERF
variants, which is a learning-based algorithm

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:26.150
tries that to reproduce real-world scenes
from only a few views.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.650
It is very challenging, look!

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:36.230
In go a bunch of photos of a scene, and the
method has to be able to synthesize new photorealistic

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.310
images between these photos.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:44.899
But this is not the only paper in this area,
researchers are very aware of the potential

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:50.090
here, and thus, a great number of NERF variants
are appearing every month.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:56.379
For instance, here is a recent one that extends
the original technique to handle shiny and

00:00:56.379 --> 00:00:58.560
reflective objects better.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.770
So, what else is there to do here?

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.220
Well, look here.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:11.429
This new one demands not a bunch of photos
from just one camera, but from 16 different

00:01:11.429 --> 00:01:12.429
cameras.

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:14.159
That’s a big ask.

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:21.069
But, in return, the method now has tons of
information about the geometry and the movement

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:28.020
of these test subjects, so, is it intelligent
enough to make something useful out of it?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:34.289
Now, believe it or not, this, in return, can
not only help us look around in the scene,

00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:37.990
but even edit it in three new ways.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:47.909
For instance, one, we can change the scale
of these subjects, add and remove them from

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:51.749
the scene, and even copy-paste them.

00:01:51.749 --> 00:01:54.380
Excellent for creating music videos.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.090
Well, talking about music videos.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.299
Do you know what is even more excellent for
those?

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:04.899
Retiming movements…that is also possible.

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:13.659
This can, for instance, improve an okay dancing
performance into an excellent one.

00:02:13.659 --> 00:02:19.239
And three, because now we are in charge of
the final footage, if the original footage

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:25.010
is shaky, well, we can choose to eliminate
that camera shake.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.219
Game changer.

00:02:26.219 --> 00:02:31.770
Still, it’s not quite the hardware requirement
where you just whip out your smartphone and

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:39.000
start nerfing and editing, but for what it
can do, it really does not ask for a lot.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:45.470
Look, if we wish to, we can even remove some
of those cameras and still expect reasonable

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:46.930
results.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.270
We lose roughly a decibel of signal per camera.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.930
Here is what that looks like.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.640
Not too shabby!

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:00.319
And all this progress just one more paper
down the line.

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:05.359
And I like the idea behind this paper a great
deal because typically what we are looking

00:03:05.359 --> 00:03:12.019
for in a followup paper is trying to achieve
similar results while asking for less data

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:13.180
from the user.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:20.090
This paper goes into the exact other direction,
and asks what amazing things could be done

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.319
if we had more data instead.

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:24.799
Loving it.

00:03:24.799 --> 00:03:31.889
And with that, not only neural view synthesis,
but neural scene editing is also possible.

00:03:31.889 --> 00:04:09.999
What a time 

00:04:09.999 --> 00:04:32.630
to be alive!

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.520
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

